family: F1
grade: deterministic

--- prompt ---
The tt_content record with uid 6 is a plugin that stores its configuration in a
FlexForm.

Which sheets does that FlexForm data structure define, and what value is actually
stored for settings.limit on that record?

--- oracle ---
echo "sheets: $(grep -oE '^[[:space:]]+<(sDEF|s[A-Z][A-Za-z]*)>' packages/bench_fixture/Configuration/FlexForms/BenchPlugin.xml | tr -d ' <>' | sort -u | tr '\n' ' ')"
echo -n "stored settings.limit on uid 6: "
ddev exec bash -c "mysql -h db -u db -pdb db -N -e \"SELECT pi_flexform FROM tt_content WHERE uid=6\"" 2>/dev/null \
    | grep -oE 'settings.limit.*?vDEF">[0-9]+' | grep -oE '[0-9]+$'

--- check ---
grep -qF 'sDEF' "$RESPONSE_FILE" || exit 1
grep -qF 'sAppearance' "$RESPONSE_FILE" || exit 1
# 9 is the stored value; 6 is the data structure's default. Answering 6 means the
# agent read the DS and never looked at the record.
grep -qE '(^|[^0-9])9([^0-9]|$)' "$RESPONSE_FILE"
